### TicketStar Auth API — Manual Testing
### Base URL: http://localhost:5010/api/auth
### Requires: API running (`dotnet run`), MySQL on port 3307, Redis on port 6380
###
### IMPORTANT: Refresh tokens are stored in httpOnly cookies by the server.
###   - VS Code REST Client: cookies are automatically sent on subsequent requests
###   - JetBrains HTTP Client: cookies are automatically sent on subsequent requests
###   - The `refresh_token` cookie is set by /register, /login, /magic-link/verify
###
### FLOW GUIDE:
###   Basic Auth:   [1] Register → [2] Login → [5] Refresh → [6] Logout
###   MFA Setup:    [2] Login → [7] MFA Setup → [8] MFA Verify Setup → [9] MFA Challenge
###   Magic Link:   [3] Magic Link Request → (check logs) → [4] Magic Link Verify
###   Cleanup:      [6] Logout  OR  [10] Revoke All Sessions

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5010/api/auth
@contentType = application/json

# ── Paste values here after running Login or Register ──────────────────────────
# Copy accessToken from the JSON response body
@accessToken = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

# Copy mfaToken from login response when mfaRequired=true
@mfaToken = PASTE_MFA_TOKEN_HERE


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GROUP 1: BASIC AUTH FLOW
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 1a. REGISTER — new account (expect 201 + accessToken + sets refresh_token cookie)
# Returns: { accessToken, expiresAt, sessionId }
# Error cases: 409 if email already registered, 400 for validation errors, 429 rate limit

POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io",
  "password": "Secure#Pass2026!",
  "fullName": "Alice Morgan"
}

###

### 1b. REGISTER — duplicate email (expect 409 "Email already registered.")

POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io",
  "password": "DifferentPass@99",
  "fullName": "Alice Duplicate"
}

###

### 1c. REGISTER — validation errors (expect 400 with field-level errors)
# Missing fullName, password too short

POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "not-a-valid-email",
  "password": "short"
}

###

### 2a. LOGIN — valid credentials, no MFA (expect 200 + accessToken + sets refresh_token cookie)
# Returns: { accessToken, expiresAt, sessionId }
# Copy accessToken → paste into @accessToken above

POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io",
  "password": "Secure#Pass2026!"
}

###

### 2b. LOGIN — wrong password (expect 401 "Invalid credentials.")
# Note: same error message regardless of whether email exists (prevents enumeration)

POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io",
  "password": "WrongPassword999"
}

###

### 2c. LOGIN — non-existent email (expect 401 "Invalid credentials." — same as wrong password)

POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nobody.exists@devmail.io",
  "password": "SomePassword123"
}

###

### 2d. LOGIN — missing required fields (expect 400 validation error)

POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io"
}

###

### 2e. BRUTE FORCE LOCKOUT TEST — run this 5+ times rapidly
# After 5 failed attempts: account locks for 15 minutes
# 6th+ attempt: expect 401 (same message — lockout not revealed)

POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io",
  "password": "BruteForceAttempt!"
}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GROUP 2: MAGIC LINK FLOW
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 3a. MAGIC LINK REQUEST — registered email (expect 200, link sent to email)
# Always returns 200 regardless of whether email exists (prevents enumeration)
# Token appears in API console logs when running in Development mode

POST {{baseUrl}}/magic-link/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io"
}

###

### 3b. MAGIC LINK REQUEST — non-existent email (expect 200 — same response, no enumeration)

POST {{baseUrl}}/magic-link/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "ghost.user@nowhere.io"
}

###

### 4a. MAGIC LINK VERIFY — valid token (expect 200 + accessToken + sets refresh_token cookie)
# Step 1: Run request 3a above
# Step 2: Check API console logs for the magic link token
# Step 3: Paste the token (the part after ?token= in the link) below
# Returns: { accessToken, expiresAt, sessionId } OR { mfaToken, mfaRequired: true }

POST {{baseUrl}}/magic-link/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "token": "PASTE_MAGIC_LINK_TOKEN_FROM_CONSOLE_LOGS_HERE"
}

###

### 4b. MAGIC LINK VERIFY — invalid/fake token (expect 401 "Invalid or used magic link.")

POST {{baseUrl}}/magic-link/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "token": "aabbccddeeff00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff00112233445566778899"
}

###

### 4c. MAGIC LINK VERIFY — already-used token (expect 401 "Invalid or used magic link.")
# Re-run request 4a after it succeeds — token is single-use

POST {{baseUrl}}/magic-link/verify
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "token": "PASTE_ALREADY_USED_TOKEN_HERE"
}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GROUP 3: GOOGLE OAUTH FLOW
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 5a. GOOGLE LOGIN — placeholder token (expect 401 "Google authentication failed.")
# To test successfully: obtain a real Google ID token from the frontend OAuth flow
# The idToken is the JWT returned by Google after the user signs in with their Google account

POST {{baseUrl}}/google-login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "idToken": "eyJhbGciOiJSUzI1NiIsImtpZCI6ImV4YW1wbGVrZXkifQ.PLACEHOLDER_GOOGLE_ID_TOKEN"
}

###

### 5b. GOOGLE LOGIN — email conflict (expect 409 "An account with this email exists...")
# This would trigger if alice.morgan@devmail.io registered with email+password
# and then tries to login via Google with the same email address

# POST {{baseUrl}}/google-login
# Content-Type: {{contentType}}
#
# {
#   "idToken": "REAL_GOOGLE_TOKEN_FOR_EXISTING_EMAIL_ACCOUNT"
# }

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GROUP 4: TOKEN MANAGEMENT
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 6a. REFRESH TOKEN — rotate access + refresh tokens (expect 200 + new accessToken)
# Reads refresh_token from httpOnly cookie (set automatically by login/register)
# Returns: { accessToken, expiresAt, sessionId }
# New refresh_token cookie is set automatically (token rotation)
# No request body needed — cookie is sent automatically by the HTTP client

POST {{baseUrl}}/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### 6b. REFRESH TOKEN — no cookie present (expect 401 "Refresh token is required.")
# Simulates a fresh client with no session

POST {{baseUrl}}/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie:

###

### 6c. REFRESH TOKEN — expired/invalid cookie value (expect 401 "Refresh token expired.")
# Simulate expired token by setting an old-looking value in Cookie header

POST {{baseUrl}}/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Cookie: refresh_token=expiredOrInvalidTokenValueHere

###

### 7. LOGOUT — revoke current session (expect 200 + clears refresh_token cookie)
# Requires: valid @accessToken from login/register (paste above)
# After this: refresh_token cookie is cleared, session deactivated
# Returns: { "message": "Logged out successfully." }

POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 8. REVOKE ALL SESSIONS — invalidate all tokens across all devices (expect 200)
# Requires: valid @accessToken
# Effect: rotates SecurityStamp, blacklists user in Redis, all JWTs immediately rejected
# All devices must re-authenticate after this call
# Returns: { "message": "All sessions revoked." }

POST {{baseUrl}}/revoke-all
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 8b. VERIFY REVOKE-ALL WORKED — reuse old token (expect 401 "Token revoked.")
# After running request 8, try using the same accessToken — should be rejected immediately
# TokenBlacklistMiddleware checks iat claim against Redis blacklist timestamp

POST {{baseUrl}}/logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GROUP 5: MFA FLOW
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### Prerequisites: be logged in (valid @accessToken from Group 1)
### Flow: [9] Setup → [10] Verify Setup → [11] Challenge (after next login) → [12] Disable

### 9. MFA SETUP — generate TOTP secret + QR code (expect 200)
# Requires: valid @accessToken
# Returns: { secret, qrCodeUri, qrCodeBase64 }
# - Scan qrCodeBase64 QR image with Google Authenticator / Authy / 1Password
# - OR enter `secret` manually into your authenticator app
# - After scanning, proceed to request 10 to complete setup

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/setup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### 10. MFA VERIFY SETUP — confirm TOTP code to activate MFA (expect 200 + recovery codes)
# Requires: valid @accessToken + 6-digit TOTP code from your authenticator app
# Returns: { recoveryCodes: ["AB3KX7YZ", ...] }  — 8 codes, shown ONCE, save them!
# After this: all future logins will require TOTP code

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/verify-setup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "code": "ENTER_6_DIGIT_TOTP_CODE_FROM_AUTHENTICATOR_APP"
}

###

### 10b. MFA VERIFY SETUP — invalid TOTP code (expect 401 "Invalid TOTP code.")

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/verify-setup
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "code": "000000"
}

###

### 11. MFA CHALLENGE — complete MFA login after step 2a returns mfaRequired:true
# Requires: @mfaToken from login response (valid for 5 minutes only)
# Code: either 6-digit TOTP from authenticator OR 8-char recovery code (e.g. "AB3KX7YZ")
# Returns: { accessToken, refreshToken, expiresAt, sessionId }
# Note: refreshToken is returned in body (httpOnly cookie support coming in future update)

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/challenge
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "mfaToken": "{{mfaToken}}",
  "code": "ENTER_6_DIGIT_TOTP_CODE_OR_8_CHAR_RECOVERY_CODE"
}

###

### 11b. MFA CHALLENGE — invalid TOTP code (expect 401 "Invalid code.")

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/challenge
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "mfaToken": "{{mfaToken}}",
  "code": "999999"
}

###

### 11c. MFA CHALLENGE — expired/invalid mfaToken (expect 401 "Invalid or expired MFA token.")

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/challenge
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "mfaToken": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.expiredOrInvalidMfaToken.fakesignature",
  "code": "123456"
}

###

### 11d. MFA CHALLENGE — using recovery code (expect 200 — recovery code consumed)
# Use one of the 8-char codes from request 10 response (e.g. "AB3KX7YZ")
# Each recovery code can only be used once

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/challenge
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "mfaToken": "{{mfaToken}}",
  "code": "PASTE_8_CHAR_RECOVERY_CODE_HERE"
}

###

### 12. MFA DISABLE — turn off MFA entirely (expect 200)
# Requires: valid @accessToken + current TOTP code OR recovery code
# After this: logins no longer require TOTP

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/disable
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "code": "ENTER_6_DIGIT_TOTP_CODE_OR_8_CHAR_RECOVERY_CODE"
}

###

### 12b. MFA DISABLE — wrong code (expect 401 "Invalid code.")

POST {{baseUrl}}/mfa/disable
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "code": "000000"
}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### GROUP 6: RATE LIMIT SCENARIOS
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 13a. RATE LIMIT — register endpoint (limit: 5 requests per 15 min per IP)
# Run this 6+ times rapidly → 6th attempt should return 429 with Retry-After header

POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "ratelimit.test{{$timestamp}}@devmail.io",
  "password": "RateLimit@Test2026",
  "fullName": "Rate Limit Tester"
}

###

### 13b. RATE LIMIT — magic link request (limit: 5 requests per 15 min per IP)
# Run this 6+ times → 6th attempt should return 429

POST {{baseUrl}}/magic-link/request
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice.morgan@devmail.io"
}

###

### 13c. RATE LIMIT — refresh endpoint (limit: 30 requests per 5 min per IP)
# Higher limit — designed to support multi-tab usage

POST {{baseUrl}}/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### NOTES FOR TESTERS
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
###
### Cookie handling:
###   VS Code REST Client & JetBrains HTTP Client automatically manage cookies.
###   The refresh_token httpOnly cookie is set by the server on login/register
###   and automatically included in subsequent requests to the same host.
###
### MFA testing tips:
###   - Use Google Authenticator, Authy, or 1Password to scan the QR from request 9
###   - TOTP codes are valid for ~90 seconds (±1 step tolerance)
###   - Recovery codes are 8 uppercase alphanumeric chars (e.g. AB3KX7YZ)
###
### Magic link token:
###   - When running the API in Development mode, the token appears in console logs
###   - Look for a log line containing "magic-link?token=" or similar
###   - Token is valid for 10 minutes and single-use
###
### Getting a Google ID token for testing:
###   - Run the frontend app and complete Google Sign-In flow
###   - Intercept the network request to /api/auth/google-login
###   - Copy the idToken value and paste into request 5a
###
### Account lockout:
###   - After 5 failed login attempts, account is locked for 15 minutes
###   - To unlock immediately: update LockedUntil to NULL in MySQL
###     psql equivalent: UPDATE Users SET LockedUntil = NULL, FailedLoginCount = 0
###     WHERE Email = 'alice.morgan@devmail.io';
###
### Redis inspection (port 6380):
###   - Token blacklist: GET user-bl:{userId}
###   - Grace period cache: KEYS grace:*
###   - Rate limit counters: KEYS rl:*
